# Privacy Policy — Duesday

**Duesday — Deadline tracker for students**
**Effective Date:** August 14, 2026

## Short Version

Your requirements, deadlines, and settings are stored **ONLY on your device**.

There are **NO accounts, no ads, no analytics, and no tracking**.

The only time anything leaves your device is when you actively use the optional **AI note scanner** or **AI priority suggestion**, which sends the specific notes or photo you choose, or the text you typed, to Google's Gemini service for one-time processing.

## 1. Local Data Storage

Duesday stores all of the following locally on your device in the app's private on-device database and preferences:

* **Requirements you add** — title, subject, type, description, deadline, estimated hours, priority, status, creation date, repeat settings, and notes.
* **App preferences** — reminder settings, calendar start-of-week, theme, and tutorial state.

We do **NOT** use user accounts, ads, analytics, or tracking scripts.

Nothing in this section is transmitted anywhere.

### Reminders and Widgets

If you enable reminders, the app schedules **local notifications** on your device. Notification permission is requested on Android 13+.

Home-screen widgets read your requirements locally.

Neither sends data anywhere.

## 2. Optional AI Features — Google Gemini API

When you use **Scan my notes** with a photo or PDF, or use an **AI priority suggestion**, the selected text, photo, or PDF is sent to Google's Gemini API for processing.

* **One-time processing only** — The request is processed on the spot and the result is shown to you. Nothing is sent when AI features are not in use.
* **Not used for training** — Per Google's standard Gemini API terms, data sent through the API is **NOT used to train Google's AI models**.
* **Retention** — Google may temporarily retain prompts and responses for up to 30 days for abuse and quality monitoring under its standard Gemini API data policies.
* **No Duesday-side storage** — We do not store or retain any AI payloads ourselves. There is no cache, no logs, and no copies beyond the local file you chose.

## 3. App Permissions

Duesday only uses permissions for the features described in this policy.

* **Internet / Network state** — used exclusively by the optional AI features above.
* **Notifications (Android 13+)** — used strictly for your local deadline reminders.
* **Photos / Files** — accessed only via the system file picker when you choose a photo or PDF to scan. The app never scans your photo gallery, and no storage permission is requested.

## 4. Data Control and Deletion

You retain full control over your data.

You can:

* **Delete individual items** anytime from a requirement's detail screen.
* **Clear all stored data** via Settings → Data → **Clear all requirements**. A one-time undo is offered immediately after.
* **Clear completed items** via Settings → Data → **Clear completed**.
* **Uninstall Duesday** to completely remove all local app data from your device.

If you've previously enabled Android's automatic app-data backup, a recent copy may exist in your Google account backup.

## 5. Children

Duesday is designed for students and does not collect personal information.

It has:

* No accounts
* No chat
* No public content

The only third-party interaction is the optional AI scanner, which processes a user-selected image, PDF, or text on demand.

## 6. Changes to This Policy

If this policy changes, the **Effective Date** above will be revised.

The updated policy will appear in the app under:

**Settings → About → Privacy Policy**

